From 5c818ace036e80b1dccf1c1c9b59f0702b3bf8a0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Quoc Cuong An <ancuong1610@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 13:46:22 +0100
Subject: Group added/deleted runs into change blocks, narrow priority, pair
 clause edits

- Stage 14: runs of >=3 consecutive ADDED/DELETED changes form change blocks
  (section_/block_ added/deleted); one review entry per block, absorbing
  counterpart-less residual groups; member records are kept
- Impact: one-sided text is high priority only when short (<=40 words) and
  normative; block members are normal priority
- Stage 07: unique ordered token containment pairs clause insertions/removals
  as MODIFIED instead of DELETED+ADDED (no threshold changes)
- Reader/API/MCP/UI: BLOCK records by default, expand_blocks toggle,
  priority filter, block polygons in the viewer

Real pair: visible findings 1365 -> 582, review queue 1289 -> 528,
high priority 812 -> 210.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
